{:lint-as {babashka.ffi/defcfn clj-kondo.lint-as/def-catch-all}

 ;; What the three public functions of spectre.core take, so that a call
 ;; with the wrong kind of argument is underlined where it is typed. Nothing
 ;; objects at run time: (derive mkey site :login) destructures the keyword
 ;; as if it were an empty map and returns the :password result.
 ;;
 ;; The options are an open map: a value of the wrong kind is caught, a
 ;; misspelt key is not.
 ;;
 ;; spectre.clipboard: a command is a vector of strings, the program first,
 ;; as in its tools table, and copy! takes the value first. A string where
 ;; the command goes, or the two swapped, is underlined.
 ;;
 ;; babashka.fs/which is the library's, annotated here because E2 calls it:
 ;; it takes the name of a program, or a path, and throws on anything else.
 ;; clj-kondo knows that tools is a vector, so (fs/which tools) and (-> tools
 ;; (fs/which)) are underlined too.
 :linters
 {:type-mismatch
  {:level :warning
   :namespaces
   {babashka.fs
    {which {:arities {1 {:args [:string]}
                      2 {:args [:string :any]}}}}
    spectre.clipboard
    {tool {:arities {0 {:ret :nilable/vector}}}
     copy! {:arities {1 {:args [:string]
                         :ret :nilable/sequential}
                      2 {:args [:string :nilable/sequential]
                         :ret :nilable/sequential}}}}
    spectre.core
    {master-key {:arities {2 {:args [:string :string]}
                           3 {:args [:string :string :keyword]}}}
     derive {:arities {2 {:args [:any :string]
                          :ret :string}
                       3 {:args [:any :string {:op :keys
                                               :opt {:counter :int
                                                     :variant :keyword
                                                     :template :keyword}}]
                          :ret :string}}}
     password {:arities {4 {:args [:string :string :string {:op :keys
                                                            :opt {:counter :int
                                                                  :variant :keyword
                                                                  :template :keyword}}]
                            :ret :string}}}}}}}}
